   "text": "I read this as a cyclosporin A\u2013type cyclic undecapeptide in which the MeBmt side chain has been modified and linked to an aryl pyrazole carrying an acrylamide.\n\n**Macrocycle.** I traced the ring from the MeBmt \u03b1-carbon: MeBmt, Abu (ethyl side chain), Sar, MeLeu, Val, MeLeu, Ala, D-Ala, MeLeu, MeLeu, MeVal, and back to MeBmt. The N-methyl groups sit on MeBmt, Sar, MeLeu (\u00d74) and MeVal, as drawn.\n\n**Modified MeBmt side chain.** The usual CH(CH\u2083)\u2013CH\u2082\u2013CH=CH\u2013CH\u2083 chain is replaced by CH(CH\u2083)\u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082CH\u2082\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013. The OH-bearing carbon is unchanged.\n\n**Linker and tail.**\n- The chain continues \u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH\u2082\u2013O\u2013 to a para-substituted phenyl ring.\n- The phenyl is bonded through N1 of a pyrazole. The pyrazole has CF\u2083 on C5 and a C(=O)NH-aryl group on C4.\n- That aryl is a benzene bearing Cl and NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH=CH\u2082 in a 1,3,5 pattern.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** The drawing shows wedges and hashes on the peptide \u03b1-carbons, the MeBmt hydroxyl carbon and the methyl-bearing carbon of the side chain. I did not re-derive each one independently. I took the stereo descriptors from the known cyclosporin A SMILES, which matches the ring as drawn, and kept the neighbour order at the modified methyl-bearing carbon.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@H]1C(=O)N(CC(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N1)[C@@H]([C@H](C)CCCC(=O)NCCNC(=O)COc1ccc(cc1)-n1ncc(C(=O)Nc2cc(Cl)cc(NC(=O)C=C)c2)c1C(F)(F)F)O)C)C(C)C)C)CC(C)C)CC(C)C)C)C)C)CC(C)C)C(C)C)CC(C)C)C)C"
